{"ts":"2026-08-07T17:21:22.188Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"42d376a0ebc79212ad1dd49b","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"1","source":"environment"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.224","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-z0cfor"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Floor polarity for the tracker measurement ratchet, with graph edge and node floors declared"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Add the second polarity to the tracker measurement ratchet so a declaration can guard a property whose good direction is up, and declare the first two floors.\n\nDelivered in scripts/release/tracker-measurement-gate.mjs: a `resolveDeclaredBound` helper that accepts exactly one of `ceiling` or `floor` and refuses zero or both; a `bound_polarity_not_declared` refusal for an ambiguous declaration and a `floor_not_a_count` refusal mirroring the existing ceiling check; `floor_undercut` and `within_floor` evaluation reasons; a floor branch in the re-baseline path that takes the maximum of declared and observed so a floor rises toward observation and is never lowered; a violation line that names its polarity and renders the shortfall as a negative distance; and a negative control that now proves both polarities fail, because a control that exercises one direction leaves the other a hypothesis.\n\nContributor attribution is deliberately restricted to ceiling violations. Contributor rows are read from the record as it stands, so they can name the mutations that pushed a population past a ceiling and can never name rows that were deleted below a floor. Claiming otherwise would be the more useful-looking behaviour and would be wrong.\n\nTwo floors declared in scripts/release/tracker-measurements.json: total deduplicated directed relationship edges, owned by pm-96h7, and total graph nodes, owned by pm-o2kc. Both were baselined from the gate's own commit view via --update at 11,318 edges and 2,368 nodes."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Task"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":1},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["area:ci","gate","governance","measurement"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-08-07T17:21:22.188Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-07T17:21:22.188Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":180},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"A declaration may carry a floor, and an observed value below it fails the gate with a distinct reason; The re-baseline path raises a floor and never lowers it, mirroring the ceiling path in the opposite direction; The negative control proves both a ceiling violation and a floor violation fail; Total deduplicated directed edges and total graph nodes are declared as floors from a commit-view measurement"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-g4k74y"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-4vz6mz","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-08-07T17:21:22.188Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-96h7","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-08-07T17:21:22.188Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-g4k74y","kind":"implements","created_at":"2026-08-07T17:21:22.188Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-ips23h","kind":"discovered_f